# Local development secrets (example).
#
# In the cluster, secrets are delivered ONLY as files on the CSI tmpfs mount
# (/mnt/secrets-store), one file per secret — never as env vars (PY-D6 / PY-R13).
# `start/setup-secrets.sh` recreates that layout locally so the same code path is exercised:
# it writes each secret to <SECRETS_MOUNT_PATH>/<SecretName>.
#
# Format: one "SecretName=value" per line. The file name on the mount == the Key Vault
# object name in the SecretProviderClass (e.g. DbConnectionString).
DbConnectionString=Server=localhost;Database=RepoUniqueNormalisedIdentifier;User Id=sa;Password=ChangeMe123!;TrustServerCertificate=True;
